Falsifies `environment_contract::verification::a_written_field_reads_back_whole`.

The defect: `write_field` records a length one past the value's, so the reader takes one byte too many.

Expected to fail: the final `assert!` (the slice read back is one byte longer than the value), for every length.

diff --git a/crates/environment_contract/src/lib.rs b/crates/environment_contract/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/environment_contract/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/environment_contract/src/lib.rs
@@ -330,7 +330,7 @@
     let bytes = value.as_bytes();
     assert!(bytes.len() <= maximum_bytes);
     let n = bytes.len();
-    page[length_offset] = n as u8;
+    page[length_offset] = n as u8 + 1;
     page[value_offset..value_offset + n].copy_from_slice(bytes);
 }
 
